  "style": {
    "id": "snap-through",
    "name": "Snap-Through",
    "description": "A bright workbench test rig for a bistable arch: a thin tempered-blue spring-steel strip clamped flat between machined steel jaws on two aluminium pedestals, bowed upward into a shallow arch, with a small aluminium tray and post on its crown and a dial gauge under it reading the deflection through a chrome plunger (red mark = the limit point). Slotted brass weights fly from a ready stack and drop down the post one at a time; each barely moves the arch, until one more passes the limit load and the strip snaps through to the other side with a short damped ring, the weights hopping ballistically on the tray. Taking every weight off leaves it flipped. The motion is the shallow two-bar (von Mises) arch: load = v^3 - v, closed form (snap.js).",
